 847+ 632B              ;speed management 2.0. starts here. Enables to set user_defined speed. Works with every MBFW.
 848+ 632B              ;the principle:
 849+ 632B              ;are you aligned?
 850+ 632B              ;NO: try to align, if not success->error. If sucess, you have AKT (=current alligned speed is ;known). Is user defined speed definied? (IX+2=255 for no user defined speed) yes, END. NO. set ;speed according to ix+2 (max up to MBFW), end
 851+ 632B              ;
 852+ 632B              ;YES:
 853+ 632B              ;is user defined speed set? (ix+2=255 or other?) NO=check if FW is 7/12? YES, align at speed
 854+ 632B              ;ix+2, end. FW is higher then 7/12, then check if AKT=IX+2? YES, end, NO, align at ix+2, END.
 855+ 632B              ;ix+2 was not 255, is FW 7/12? YES, then set FWmax, end. NO the is AKT=MBFW max? YES, then END
 856+ 632B              ;NO, then align at FW max speed, end
 857+ 632B              ;output: ix+7= 0-23 if speed set, or 255 if not set
 858+ 632B
 859+ 632B              ;SM20 uses:
 860+ 632B              ;bit 4,(ix+0)	PRINT or not to PRINT
 861+ 632B              ;(ix+8)		contains maximum speed by detected MBFW (7, 12 or 23)
 862+ 632B              ;(ix+6)		timeout value
 863+ 632B              ;bit 6,(ix+0)	state of speed alignment between uart& module, 0 not aligned
 864+ 632B              ;bit 5,(ix+0)	state of module connection to AP, 0 not connected to AP
