2820+ 6B91              ; search_by_Busy_dir_slow
2821+ 6B91              ; Fully bank-safe fallback. It is used only when a file name itself crosses a
2822+ 6B91              ; #FFFF -> #C000 directory-page boundary. Such names are rare, so paging cost
2823+ 6B91              ; no longer slows down every ordinary FIND operation.
2824+ 6B91              ;
2825+ 6B91              ; One-character FIND is handled before this fallback and compares only the
2826+ 6B91              ; first character.  This slow path therefore normally handles 2+ character
2827+ 6B91              ; substring searches whose source name crosses a directory-bank boundary.
2828+ 6B91              ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
2829+ 6B91              search_by_Busy_dir_slow:
