8184+ 8421              ;OUT=A=4= starting item ".."
8185+ 8421              ;bits 1 (items 0=abbreviated, 1= full) and 3 (current command type 0=LIST, 1=NLST) from flag_dir are of interest here
8186+ 8421              get_item_name
8187+ 8421              ;128K bank-safe parser.
8188+ 8421              ;IN: callers currently use SCF; C/NC is kept only for source compatibility.
8189+ 8421              ;OUT=HL=name start in banked directory RAM
8190+ 8421              ;    BC=16-bit name length
8191+ 8421              ;    DE=16-bit file length for LIST abbreviated (0 for NLST/"..")
8192+ 8421              ;    item_name_page=page-table pointer belonging to returned HL
8193+ 8421              ;OUT=A=0 directory, A=1 file, A=2 NLST unknown type,
8194+ 8421              ;      A=3 LIST full/malformed, A=4 synthetic ".."
8195+ 8421              ;
8196+ 8421              ;No temporary zero is written into the directory. The parser uses the stored
8197+ 8421              ;16-bit item length as its boundary, so an item/name may cross 16K pages and
8198+ 8421              ;may also be longer than 255 bytes.
